module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Held.CentralCovers.TwoPrimary.BinaryRelators.Normalization
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Held.CentralCovers.TwoPrimary.BinaryRelators.RemainingDefects.Centralizer
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Held.CentralCovers.TwoPrimary.BinaryRelators.RemainingDefects.CosetMembership.Interpretation
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Held.CentralCovers.TwoPrimary.BinaryRelators.RemainingDefects.CosetMembership.Certificate

/-!+# Held's centralizer word belongs to the explicit seed subgroup

The retained Todd–Coxeter discovery connects the representative of
`t = y³[x,y³]²` to the identity coset. Its dependency slice is expanded into
ordinary Lean proofs: defining transitions are reflexivity, relator scans
use composition and cancellation, and conflicting transitions give equalities.
The certificate holds in every word-action system with the literal source
loops. `Interpretation` realizes such a system on the actual right cosets of
`centralizerSpan z x y`; the possibly nontrivial central relators are valid
loops because the subgroup contains `z`.

Source: John Bray's ATLAS `HeG1-P1.M`, retained in `Held/Model/Source/`.
Only its literal words are used. No assertion about presentation faithfulness,
the multiplier, or a concrete Held permutation representation enters the proof.
The certificate's reproduction data and checking measurements are recorded in
`CosetMembership/source/README.md`.
-/

namespace Held.CentralCovers.TwoPrimary.BinaryRelators.RemainingDefects
variable {E : Type*} [Group E]

set_option linter.unusedVariables false in
/-- The source centralizer word lies in the subgroup generated by the nine
explicit seeds and the common central binary defect. The exact relators remain
in the consumer interface; the certificate itself only needs central loops. -/
public theorem centralizerWord_mem (z x y : E) (h : Normalized z x y)
    (h0 : Held.relationWord x y 0 = 1) (h5 : Held.relationWord x y 5 = 1) :
    centralizerWord x y ∈ centralizerSpan z x y :=
  CosetMembership.membership_of_action z x y h
    (fun _ s => CosetMembership.target_fixes_origin s)

end Held.CentralCovers.TwoPrimary.BinaryRelators.RemainingDefects
